# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Training archives.
#
# The rules above (features.jsonl, labels.jsonl, tier2_shadow.jsonl, ...) are
# BASENAME patterns, so they match those files ANYWHERE in the tree — including
# the dated archive copies, which is not intended. `git add` on them is then a
# silent no-op. These negations re-include the archived copies and must stay
# BELOW those rules to take effect.
#
# Compact feature/label/outcome files are tracked so the trainable core is
# durable. Bulk raw capture stays local: screened_alerts ~4MB/day and logs
# ~5MB/day would bloat the repo without adding signal.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!archive/*/data/*.jsonl
!archive/*/data/*.json
archive/*/data/screened_alerts.jsonl
archive/*/logs/
venv_sentiment/
.news_digest_state.json
